  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Finely chop or crush garlic. In a medium saucepan, melt 1/2 the butter over medium heat. Cook 1/2 the garlic until fragrant, 1 min. Add basmati rice, water (for the rice), stir, cover with a lid and reduce heat to low.\n• Cook for 10 mins, then remove from heat and keep covered until rice is tender and the water absorbed, 10 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/63f7f31f98df5e794d0b7343/step-4b6d3ba2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, cut capsicum into bite-sized pieces. Thinly cut zucchini into half moons. Drain and rinse black beans.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/63f7f31f98df5e794d0b7343/step-ac38d24e.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a large frying pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat. Cook capsicum until softened, 4-5 mins. Add zucchini and black beans. Cook until tender, 2-3 mins.\n• Stir in Mexican seasoning, tomato paste, the sugar, and the remaining butter and garlic and cook until fragrant, 1 min.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/63f7f31f98df5e794d0b7343/step-0feb9212.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Add water (for the sauce) and vegetable stock powder. Reduce heat to low and simmer until slightly thickened, 3-4 mins. Season to taste.\n• Divide rice between bowls and top with black bean chilli. Tear over coriander. Garnish with chilli flakes (if using).\n• Serve with sour cream.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/63f7f31f98df5e794d0b7343/step-b7c45425.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
